["<aside class=\"callout why\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Why it matters</div><p>A blood trail at dusk, a twisted knee, fog on the ridge: one day you will sleep out. Shelter is what makes that a cold night, not a rescue.</p></aside><figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"The ground steals the most heat when you lie on it: a person on bare ground loses heat straight down; a person on a thick bed of boughs or a pad keeps it. Insulate under you first, then over you.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">The ground steals the most heat</text><rect x=\"0\" y=\"200\" width=\"400\" height=\"100\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/><rect x=\"106\" y=\"185\" width=\"55\" height=\"15\" rx=\"5.5\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><line x1=\"161\" y1=\"193\" x2=\"201\" y2=\"194\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"8.8\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><circle cx=\"95\" cy=\"190\" r=\"9.9\" fill=\"#d9b48f\"/><line x1=\"100\" y1=\"204\" x2=\"100\" y2=\"240\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><polygon points=\"100,250 106,240 94,240\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\"/><line x1=\"130\" y1=\"204\" x2=\"130\" y2=\"240\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><polygon points=\"130,250 136,240 124,240\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\"/><line x1=\"160\" y1=\"204\" x2=\"160\" y2=\"240\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><polygon points=\"160,250 166,240 154,240\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\"/><line x1=\"190\" y1=\"204\" x2=\"190\" y2=\"240\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><polygon points=\"190,250 196,240 184,240\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\"/><text x=\"150\" y=\"280\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#c0392b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">On bare ground</text><rect x=\"240\" y=\"186\" width=\"140\" height=\"14\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/><rect x=\"284\" y=\"173\" width=\"45\" height=\"13\" rx=\"4.5\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><line x1=\"329\" y1=\"181\" x2=\"361\" y2=\"182\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"7.2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><circle cx=\"275\" cy=\"178\" r=\"8.1\" fill=\"#d9b48f\"/><text x=\"310\" y=\"230\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2e7d32\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Thick bed under</text><text x=\"310\" y=\"250\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#2e7d32\" text-anchor=\"middle\">heat stays in</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"60\" font-size=\"17\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Insulate under you first</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"82\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">then over you</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Bed under you first, roof over you second (Tip).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: what this session covers</summary><ul><li>Choosing a spot, insulating from the ground, a tarp shelter, a debris hut, foil blankets versus bivy bags, using fire with shelter, the night routine, and sharing heat.</li><li>Why you lose heat: <a href=\"#/s/cold-injuries/0\">Cold injuries</a>. Fire: <a href=\"#/s/fire-wet-weather/0\">Fire in wet weather</a>. Being found: <a href=\"#/s/lost-survival-kit/0\">Lost</a>.</li><li>Assumption: October nights near 0 °C in the Kamloops hills, wet nights near 5 °C in the Fraser Valley.</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Pick the spot: a sheltered bench part way up the slope, near trees and firewood, is best. Avoid the valley bottom where cold air pools, the windy ridge top, and anything under a dead tree that can fall.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Pick the spot</text><path d=\"M0 230 L120 150 L200 175 L290 120 L400 160 L400 300 L0 300 Z\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/><path d=\"M200 175 L200 300\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"3\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-dasharray=\"6 6\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"290\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\" text-anchor=\"middle\">cold air pools low</text><rect x=\"57\" y=\"182\" width=\"6\" height=\"14\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><polygon points=\"60,126 44,182 76,182\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/><rect x=\"97\" y=\"160\" width=\"6\" height=\"12\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><polygon points=\"100,112 86,160 114,160\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/><line x1=\"330\" y1=\"136\" x2=\"330\" y2=\"70\" stroke=\"#8b5a2b\" stroke-width=\"6\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><line x1=\"330\" y1=\"80\" x2=\"350\" y2=\"66\" stroke=\"#8b5a2b\" stroke-width=\"4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><line x1=\"352\" y1=\"54\" x2=\"368\" y2=\"70\" stroke=\"#c0392b\" stroke-width=\"4.5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><line x1=\"368\" y1=\"54\" x2=\"352\" y2=\"70\" stroke=\"#c0392b\" stroke-width=\"4.5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><text x=\"330\" y=\"56\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#c0392b\" text-anchor=\"end\">dead tree</text><circle cx=\"150\" cy=\"164\" r=\"9.0\" fill=\"#2e7d32\"/><path d=\"M138 140 l10 10 l17 -19\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#2e7d32\" stroke-width=\"6.0\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><text x=\"130\" y=\"80\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2e7d32\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Bench part way up</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"98\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">near trees and fuel</text><text x=\"290\" y=\"108\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">windy top</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Start building at least an hour before dark (Tip).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: the 8 key points in full</summary><ol><li>Insulation and a barrier from the ground and weather are the core of preventing and treating hypothermia (75%, Wilderness Medical Society via American Family Physician).</li><li>The ground pulls heat by conduction. A thick bed matters more than a roof on a dry night (75%, physics; Tip on the order).</li><li>Wind and wet speed heat loss a lot <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li>Cold air sinks into valley bottoms at night (75%, see <a href=\"#/s/wind-thermals/0\">Wind and thermals</a>).</li><li>A tarp or bivy is faster and safer than building from the bush when tired or hurt <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>.</li><li>Foil blankets reflect radiant heat but do little against conduction from the ground <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>.</li><li>A shelter hidden in thick timber can hide you from searchers. Put a signal in the open <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>.</li><li>Two people sharing one bed and cover stay warmer (Tip).</li></ol></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Pick the spot: a sheltered bench part way up the slope, near trees and firewood, is best. Avoid the valley bottom where cold air pools, the windy ridge top, and anything under a dead tree that can fall.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Pick the spot</text><path d=\"M0 230 L120 150 L200 175 L290 120 L400 160 L400 300 L0 300 Z\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/><path d=\"M200 175 L200 300\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"3\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-dasharray=\"6 6\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"290\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\" text-anchor=\"middle\">cold air pools low</text><rect x=\"57\" y=\"182\" width=\"6\" height=\"14\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><polygon points=\"60,126 44,182 76,182\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/><rect x=\"97\" y=\"160\" width=\"6\" height=\"12\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><polygon points=\"100,112 86,160 114,160\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/><line x1=\"330\" y1=\"136\" x2=\"330\" y2=\"70\" stroke=\"#8b5a2b\" stroke-width=\"6\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><line x1=\"330\" y1=\"80\" x2=\"350\" y2=\"66\" stroke=\"#8b5a2b\" stroke-width=\"4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><line x1=\"352\" y1=\"54\" x2=\"368\" y2=\"70\" stroke=\"#c0392b\" stroke-width=\"4.5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><line x1=\"368\" y1=\"54\" x2=\"352\" y2=\"70\" stroke=\"#c0392b\" stroke-width=\"4.5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><text x=\"330\" y=\"56\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#c0392b\" text-anchor=\"end\">dead tree</text><circle cx=\"150\" cy=\"164\" r=\"9.0\" fill=\"#2e7d32\"/><path d=\"M138 140 l10 10 l17 -19\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#2e7d32\" stroke-width=\"6.0\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><text x=\"130\" y=\"80\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2e7d32\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Bench part way up</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"98\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">near trees and fuel</text><text x=\"290\" y=\"108\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">windy top</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Bench part way up, near trees and fuel. Not the valley floor (Tip).</li><li>Look up: no dead trees or hanging branches (Tip).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: choosing a site in full</summary><ul><li>Choose the driest spot you can, out of the wind, away from low points where cold air and water collect (65%, shelter guides via search).</li><li>Cold air sinks downhill at night and pools in draws and valley floors (75%, thermals, <a href=\"#/s/wind-thermals/0\">Wind and thermals</a>).</li><li>Ridge tops are windy (Tip).</li><li>Look up for dead standing trees and broken branches that can fall in wind (Tip).</li><li>Not in a gully, a creek bottom or an avalanche path. See <a href=\"#/s/avalanche-hunters/0\">Avalanche awareness</a> (Tip).</li><li>Near firewood and water, and near an opening where you can be seen (Tip).</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram anim\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Animation: red heat dots drain down out of a person lying on bare ground, while a person on a thick bed of boughs keeps the heat dots near the body. Bed first, roof second.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Bare ground vs a bed</text><rect x=\"0\" y=\"200\" width=\"400\" height=\"100\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/><rect x=\"74\" y=\"187\" width=\"45\" height=\"13\" rx=\"4.5\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><line x1=\"119\" y1=\"195\" x2=\"151\" y2=\"196\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"7.2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><circle cx=\"65\" cy=\"192\" r=\"8.1\" fill=\"#d9b48f\"/><rect x=\"230\" y=\"184\" width=\"150\" height=\"16\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/><rect x=\"284\" y=\"171\" width=\"45\" height=\"13\" rx=\"4.5\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><line x1=\"329\" y1=\"179\" x2=\"361\" y2=\"180\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"7.2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><circle cx=\"275\" cy=\"176\" r=\"8.1\" fill=\"#d9b48f\"/><g><animateTransform attributeName=\"transform\" type=\"translate\" values=\"0 0;0 50\" dur=\"1.5s\" repeatCount=\"4\" begin=\"0.0s\"/><circle cx=\"80\" cy=\"210\" r=\"6.0\" fill=\"#c0392b\"/></g><g><animateTransform attributeName=\"transform\" type=\"translate\" values=\"0 0;0 50\" dur=\"1.5s\" repeatCount=\"4\" begin=\"0.3s\"/><circle cx=\"110\" cy=\"210\" r=\"6.0\" fill=\"#c0392b\"/></g><g><animateTransform attributeName=\"transform\" type=\"translate\" values=\"0 0;0 50\" dur=\"1.5s\" repeatCount=\"4\" begin=\"0.6s\"/><circle cx=\"140\" cy=\"210\" r=\"6.0\" fill=\"#c0392b\"/></g><g><animateTransform attributeName=\"transform\" type=\"translate\" values=\"0 0;0 12;0 0\" dur=\"1.5s\" repeatCount=\"4\" begin=\"0.0s\"/><circle cx=\"290\" cy=\"170\" r=\"6.0\" fill=\"#c0392b\"/></g><g><animateTransform attributeName=\"transform\" type=\"translate\" values=\"0 0;0 12;0 0\" dur=\"1.5s\" repeatCount=\"4\" begin=\"0.3s\"/><circle cx=\"320\" cy=\"170\" r=\"6.0\" fill=\"#c0392b\"/></g><g><animateTransform attributeName=\"transform\" type=\"translate\" values=\"0 0;0 12;0 0\" dur=\"1.5s\" repeatCount=\"4\" begin=\"0.6s\"/><circle cx=\"350\" cy=\"170\" r=\"6.0\" fill=\"#c0392b\"/></g><g opacity=\"0\"><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" values=\"0;1\" begin=\"1s\" dur=\"0.4s\" fill=\"freeze\"/><text x=\"110\" y=\"110\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#c0392b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Heat drains down</text></g><g opacity=\"0\"><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" values=\"0;1\" begin=\"2s\" dur=\"0.4s\" fill=\"freeze\"/><text x=\"310\" y=\"110\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2e7d32\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Bed stops it</text></g><g opacity=\"0\"><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" values=\"0;1\" begin=\"6s\" dur=\"0.4s\" fill=\"freeze\"/><rect x=\"89\" y=\"262\" width=\"221\" height=\"30\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"283\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Bed first, roof second</text></g>\n</svg>\n<figcaption>Heat drains into bare ground. A thick bed stops it. <button class=\"anim-replay\">↻ Replay</button></figcaption></figure><ul><li>Thicker than you think. It squashes flat under you (Tip).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: the bed in full</summary><ul><li>Insulate the ground contact area: it is one of the key places to protect (75%, Wilderness Medical Society via American Family Physician).</li><li>Bed materials (Tip): closed cell foam pad, your pack, spruce or fir boughs, dry grass, dry leaves, layered thick.</li><li>Build it so it is still a hand or more thick when you lie on it (Tip).</li><li>Sit on your pack while building to stay off the ground (Tip).</li><li>Cutting boughs: take a few from many trees, not one tree stripped. Check land rules where you are (Tip).</li></ul></details>","<div class=\"steps\" data-n=\"4\"><div class=\"steps-head\"><b>Tarp shelter in 4 steps</b><span class=\"steps-count\">1 of 4</span></div><div class=\"steps-track\"><figure class=\"step-frame\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Tarp step 1: tie a cord between two trees about waist to chest high, tight.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">1. Ridgeline between trees</text><rect x=\"0\" y=\"230\" width=\"400\" height=\"70\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/><rect x=\"57\" y=\"198\" width=\"6\" height=\"32\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><polygon points=\"60,70 24,198 96,198\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/><rect x=\"337\" y=\"198\" width=\"6\" height=\"32\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><polygon points=\"340,70 304,198 376,198\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/><line x1=\"70\" y1=\"150\" x2=\"330\" y2=\"150\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"3\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"140\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Cord, tight</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"288\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Cord between two trees</text>\n</svg>\n<figcaption><b>1.</b> Tie a tight cord between two trees.</figcaption></figure><figure class=\"step-frame\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Tarp step 2: drape the tarp over the cord.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">2. Drape the tarp</text><rect x=\"0\" y=\"230\" width=\"400\" height=\"70\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/><rect x=\"57\" y=\"198\" width=\"6\" height=\"32\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><polygon points=\"60,70 24,198 96,198\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/><rect x=\"337\" y=\"198\" width=\"6\" height=\"32\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><polygon points=\"340,70 304,198 376,198\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/><line x1=\"70\" y1=\"150\" x2=\"330\" y2=\"150\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"3\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><polygon points=\"110,150 290,150 290,226 110,226\" fill=\"#4f7a52\" opacity=\".85\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"288\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Over the cord</text>\n</svg>\n<figcaption><b>2.</b> Drape the tarp over the cord.</figcaption></figure><figure class=\"step-frame\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Tarp step 3: pull the windward edge down to the ground and pin it with rocks or stakes. Open side away from the wind.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">3. Low to the wind</text><rect x=\"0\" y=\"230\" width=\"400\" height=\"70\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/><rect x=\"57\" y=\"198\" width=\"6\" height=\"32\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><polygon points=\"60,70 24,198 96,198\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/><rect x=\"337\" y=\"198\" width=\"6\" height=\"32\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><polygon points=\"340,70 304,198 376,198\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/><polygon points=\"110,150 290,150 330,230 70,230\" fill=\"#4f7a52\"/><line x1=\"390\" y1=\"120\" x2=\"330\" y2=\"154\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><polygon points=\"320,160 334,160 327,148\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\"/><text x=\"370\" y=\"100\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\" text-anchor=\"middle\">wind</text><circle cx=\"80\" cy=\"230\" r=\"8.0\" fill=\"#9a9a8f\"/><circle cx=\"320\" cy=\"230\" r=\"8.0\" fill=\"#9a9a8f\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"288\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Windward edge pinned low</text>\n</svg>\n<figcaption><b>3.</b> Pin the windward edge low.</figcaption></figure><figure class=\"step-frame\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Tarp step 4: build a thick bed of boughs or your pack and foam pad under the tarp before dark.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">4. Bed under it</text><rect x=\"0\" y=\"230\" width=\"400\" height=\"70\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/><polygon points=\"110,150 290,150 330,230 70,230\" fill=\"#4f7a52\" opacity=\".55\"/><rect x=\"110\" y=\"214\" width=\"180\" height=\"16\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/><rect x=\"164\" y=\"201\" width=\"45\" height=\"13\" rx=\"4.5\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><line x1=\"209\" y1=\"209\" x2=\"241\" y2=\"210\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"7.2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><circle cx=\"155\" cy=\"206\" r=\"8.1\" fill=\"#d9b48f\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"120\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Bed before dark</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"288\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Thick bed, then crawl in</text>\n</svg>\n<figcaption><b>4.</b> Build the bed under it before dark.</figcaption></figure></div><div class=\"steps-nav\"><button class=\"steps-prev\" aria-label=\"Back\">‹ Back</button><span class=\"steps-dots\"><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i></span><button class=\"steps-next\" aria-label=\"Next\">Next ›</button></div></div><ul><li>A 2 m by 3 m tarp and 10 m of cord cover two people (Tip).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: tarp in full</summary><ul><li>Tarps and bivy bags are among the most effective shelter tools for their weight, and often safer than building when tired, hurt or short of light (65%, shelter guides via search).</li><li>Open side away from the wind. Windward side pinned to the ground with rocks, logs or stakes (Tip).</li><li>Steep pitch sheds rain and snow (Tip).</li><li>Carry a light tarp in the day pack in October (Tip). An emergency bivy bag works alone if you have no tarp.</li><li>Lean to version: tie only the top edge to the cord and stake the bottom edge on the windward side. More open, good with a fire in front (Tip).</li></ul></details>","<div class=\"tbl\"><table><thead><tr><th></th><th>Foil blanket</th><th>Bivy bag</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Weight</td><td>Very light</td><td>Light</td></tr><tr><td>Stops wind</td><td>If wrapped well</td><td>Yes</td></tr><tr><td>Stops ground cold</td><td>No</td><td>A little</td></tr><tr><td>Tears</td><td>Easily</td><td>Less</td></tr><tr><td>My lean</td><td>Backup</td><td>Carry this</td></tr></tbody></table></div><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: what the sources say</summary><ul><li>Foil blankets reflect radiant heat, but the \"reflects 90%\" claim on packets is marketing <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>.</li><li>The thin film does almost nothing against conduction into the ground (65%, medical equipment supplier and gear reviews).</li><li>They need an air gap to work against radiation; touching skin, they act like a thin plastic sheet <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">60%</span>.</li><li>They do not breathe: moisture gets trapped <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">60%</span>.</li><li>A bag shape (bivy) wraps you fully and stops wind; you still need a pad or bed under it (Tip).</li><li>My lean: carry an emergency bivy bag in the pack and a foil blanket in the pocket kit.</li></ul></details>","<div class=\"steps\" data-n=\"4\"><div class=\"steps-head\"><b>Debris hut in 4 steps</b><span class=\"steps-count\">1 of 4</span></div><div class=\"steps-track\"><figure class=\"step-frame\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Debris hut step 1: rest one end of a long pole on a stump or low branch, the other end on the ground, a little longer than you.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">1. Ridgepole on a stump</text><rect x=\"0\" y=\"230\" width=\"400\" height=\"70\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/><rect x=\"60\" y=\"180\" width=\"30\" height=\"50\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><line x1=\"75\" y1=\"182\" x2=\"340\" y2=\"228\" stroke=\"#8b5a2b\" stroke-width=\"9\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><text x=\"220\" y=\"160\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">A bit longer than you</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"288\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Pole from stump to ground</text>\n</svg>\n<figcaption><b>1.</b> Pole from a stump to the ground.</figcaption></figure><figure class=\"step-frame\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Debris hut step 2: lean sticks along both sides of the pole like ribs, close together.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">2. Ribs both sides</text><rect x=\"0\" y=\"230\" width=\"400\" height=\"70\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/><rect x=\"60\" y=\"180\" width=\"30\" height=\"50\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><line x1=\"75\" y1=\"182\" x2=\"340\" y2=\"228\" stroke=\"#8b5a2b\" stroke-width=\"9\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><line x1=\"90\" y1=\"186\" x2=\"80\" y2=\"230\" stroke=\"#8b5a2b\" stroke-width=\"4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><line x1=\"112\" y1=\"190\" x2=\"102\" y2=\"230\" stroke=\"#8b5a2b\" stroke-width=\"4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><line x1=\"134\" y1=\"193\" x2=\"124\" y2=\"230\" stroke=\"#8b5a2b\" stroke-width=\"4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><line x1=\"156\" y1=\"197\" x2=\"146\" y2=\"230\" stroke=\"#8b5a2b\" stroke-width=\"4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><line x1=\"178\" y1=\"200\" x2=\"168\" y2=\"230\" stroke=\"#8b5a2b\" stroke-width=\"4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><line x1=\"200\" y1=\"204\" x2=\"190\" y2=\"230\" stroke=\"#8b5a2b\" stroke-width=\"4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><line x1=\"222\" y1=\"208\" x2=\"212\" y2=\"230\" stroke=\"#8b5a2b\" stroke-width=\"4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><line x1=\"244\" y1=\"211\" x2=\"234\" y2=\"230\" stroke=\"#8b5a2b\" stroke-width=\"4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><line x1=\"266\" y1=\"215\" x2=\"256\" y2=\"230\" stroke=\"#8b5a2b\" stroke-width=\"4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><line x1=\"288\" y1=\"218\" x2=\"278\" y2=\"230\" stroke=\"#8b5a2b\" stroke-width=\"4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><line x1=\"310\" y1=\"222\" x2=\"300\" y2=\"230\" stroke=\"#8b5a2b\" stroke-width=\"4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"288\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Close ribs, small gaps</text>\n</svg>\n<figcaption><b>2.</b> Lean close ribs along both sides.</figcaption></figure><figure class=\"step-frame\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Debris hut step 3: pile leaves, needles and boughs thick over the ribs. Thicker is warmer.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">3. Pile it thick</text><rect x=\"0\" y=\"230\" width=\"400\" height=\"70\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/><path d=\"M60 230 Q70 150 200 170 Q330 190 350 230 Z\" fill=\"#9a7b4f\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"120\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Thick as your arm is long</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"140\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">(Tip)</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"288\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Pile it thick</text>\n</svg>\n<figcaption><b>3.</b> Pile leaves and boughs thick.</figcaption></figure><figure class=\"step-frame\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Debris hut step 4: fill the inside with dry leaves and needles too, crawl in feet first, and plug the door with a pack or a pile.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">4. Stuff the inside</text><rect x=\"0\" y=\"230\" width=\"400\" height=\"70\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/><path d=\"M60 230 Q70 150 200 170 Q330 190 350 230 Z\" fill=\"#9a7b4f\"/><rect x=\"90\" y=\"200\" width=\"200\" height=\"26\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#c8a46a\"/><circle cx=\"80\" cy=\"212\" r=\"9.0\" fill=\"#d9b48f\"/><rect x=\"36\" y=\"200\" width=\"30\" height=\"30\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text x=\"52\" y=\"186\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">door plug</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"288\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Bed inside too. Plug the door</text>\n</svg>\n<figcaption><b>4.</b> Fill the inside, crawl in, plug the door.</figcaption></figure></div><div class=\"steps-nav\"><button class=\"steps-prev\" aria-label=\"Back\">‹ Back</button><span class=\"steps-dots\"><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i></span><button class=\"steps-next\" aria-label=\"Next\">Next ›</button></div></div><ul><li>Takes hours and lots of material. Start early <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: debris hut in full</summary><ul><li>Debris shelters can give emergency insulation when time is short, but they are uncomfortable and need large amounts of dry material (65%, shelter guides via search).</li><li>Make it just big enough for you: a small space warms faster (Tip).</li><li>Thickness: \"as thick as your arm is long\" is a common bushcraft rule (Tip, not tested here).</li><li>In the dry Interior you may not find enough leaves. Boughs and needles work (Tip).</li><li>My lean: a tarp in the pack beats 3 hours of building.</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Fire plus a reflector wall: a wall of stacked logs behind the fire bounces heat back toward the person lying on a bed on the other side. Keep the fire small with a safe gap, and check the fire rules.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Fire plus reflector wall</text><rect x=\"0\" y=\"220\" width=\"400\" height=\"80\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/><rect x=\"290\" y=\"140\" width=\"24\" height=\"80\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><rect x=\"318\" y=\"140\" width=\"24\" height=\"80\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><text x=\"316\" y=\"128\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Log wall</text><line x1=\"214\" y1=\"214\" x2=\"262\" y2=\"206\" stroke=\"#8b5a2b\" stroke-width=\"9.0\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><line x1=\"218\" y1=\"206\" x2=\"266\" y2=\"214\" stroke=\"#8b5a2b\" stroke-width=\"9.0\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><path d=\"M226 206 Q221 182 240 161 Q259 182 254 206 Z\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><path d=\"M233 206 Q230 193 240 180 Q250 193 247 206 Z\" fill=\"#f6c344\"/><rect x=\"40\" y=\"204\" width=\"120\" height=\"14\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/><rect x=\"78\" y=\"193\" width=\"40\" height=\"11\" rx=\"4.0\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><line x1=\"118\" y1=\"199\" x2=\"147\" y2=\"200\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"6.4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><circle cx=\"70\" cy=\"197\" r=\"7.2\" fill=\"#d9b48f\"/><line x1=\"250\" y1=\"160\" x2=\"168\" y2=\"178\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"3\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><polygon points=\"160,180 169,183 167,174\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><line x1=\"280\" y1=\"180\" x2=\"178\" y2=\"195\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"3\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><polygon points=\"170,196 179,200 177,190\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text x=\"140\" y=\"120\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Heat bounces back</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"288\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Small fire, safe gap, check the rules</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Small fire, safe gap, and only when fire is legal <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: fire and shelter in full</summary><ul><li>A wall of logs or rocks behind the fire bounces heat toward you (Tip).</li><li>Keep the fire small and the tarp high above and away (Tip). See <a href=\"#/s/fire-wet-weather/0\">Fire</a> for the size limit and ban checks <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li>Feed it through the night, or let it die and rely on the bed. A big fire next to a sleeping hunter is how sleeping bags and tarps burn (Tip).</li><li>Carbon monoxide: never burn a stove or fire inside a closed shelter (Tip).</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Night routine for an unplanned night: eat before sleep, pee before sleep, put on dry socks and dry wet ones inside your shirt, keep the toque on all night, keep boots in a bag so they do not freeze, and when cold, clench muscles, eat and move.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Night routine</text><rect x=\"20\" y=\"46\" width=\"112\" height=\"90\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"76\" y=\"86\" font-size=\"17\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Eat</text><text x=\"76\" y=\"110\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">before sleep</text><rect x=\"145\" y=\"46\" width=\"112\" height=\"90\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"201\" y=\"86\" font-size=\"17\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Pee</text><text x=\"201\" y=\"110\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">before sleep</text><rect x=\"270\" y=\"46\" width=\"112\" height=\"90\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"326\" y=\"86\" font-size=\"17\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Dry socks</text><text x=\"326\" y=\"110\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">wet in shirt</text><rect x=\"20\" y=\"150\" width=\"112\" height=\"90\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"76\" y=\"190\" font-size=\"17\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Toque on</text><text x=\"76\" y=\"214\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">all night</text><rect x=\"145\" y=\"150\" width=\"112\" height=\"90\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"201\" y=\"190\" font-size=\"17\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Boots</text><text x=\"201\" y=\"214\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">in a bag, not out</text><rect x=\"270\" y=\"150\" width=\"112\" height=\"90\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"326\" y=\"190\" font-size=\"17\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Cold?</text><text x=\"326\" y=\"214\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">eat, move</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"285\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Small habits, warmer night</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Food is fuel. Eat before you sleep (Tip).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: the routine in full</summary><ul><li>All Tip unless marked:<ul><li>Eat something with fat before sleeping. Shivering burns fuel.</li><li>Pee before you settle. Holding it costs heat.</li><li>Dry socks on. Wet socks inside your shirt to dry from body heat.</li><li>Toque and buff on all night. Hood up.</li><li>Boots in a bag or under you, so they do not freeze stiff.</li><li>Cold in the night: clench big muscles, eat, sit up and move, add a layer.</li></ul></li><li>Keep the headlamp and whistle in a pocket you can find in the dark (Tip).</li><li>Keep the phone warm for the morning check in. See <a href=\"#/s/lost-survival-kit/0\">Lost</a>.</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Two hunters share heat: lie back to back on one bed under one cover. Two bodies, one roof.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Two hunters: share heat</text><rect x=\"0\" y=\"220\" width=\"400\" height=\"80\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/><rect x=\"80\" y=\"206\" width=\"240\" height=\"14\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/><rect x=\"110\" y=\"186\" width=\"80\" height=\"20\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><circle cx=\"100\" cy=\"194\" r=\"9.0\" fill=\"#d9b48f\"/><rect x=\"200\" y=\"186\" width=\"80\" height=\"20\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#7c5a99\"/><circle cx=\"290\" cy=\"194\" r=\"9.0\" fill=\"#d9b48f\"/><path d=\"M90 182 Q200 120 310 182\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#4f7a52\" stroke-width=\"8\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"100\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Back to back, one bed</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"120\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">one cover over both</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"285\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Two bodies, one roof</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>One bed, one cover, back to back (Tip).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: sharing heat in full</summary><ul><li>Two people huddling share body heat. In cold water, huddling is a taught technique (75%, see <a href=\"#/s/water-safety/0\">Water safety</a>). On land, the same idea works under one cover (Tip).</li><li>Put the colder or hurt person in the middle of all the insulation (Tip).</li><li>Swap who gets up to feed the fire (Tip).</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"The ground steals the most heat when you lie on it: a person on bare ground loses heat straight down; a person on a thick bed of boughs or a pad keeps it. Insulate under you first, then over you.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">The ground steals the most heat</text><rect x=\"0\" y=\"200\" width=\"400\" height=\"100\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/><rect x=\"106\" y=\"185\" width=\"55\" height=\"15\" rx=\"5.5\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><line x1=\"161\" y1=\"193\" x2=\"201\" y2=\"194\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"8.8\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><circle cx=\"95\" cy=\"190\" r=\"9.9\" fill=\"#d9b48f\"/><line x1=\"100\" y1=\"204\" x2=\"100\" y2=\"240\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><polygon points=\"100,250 106,240 94,240\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\"/><line x1=\"130\" y1=\"204\" x2=\"130\" y2=\"240\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><polygon points=\"130,250 136,240 124,240\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\"/><line x1=\"160\" y1=\"204\" x2=\"160\" y2=\"240\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><polygon points=\"160,250 166,240 154,240\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\"/><line x1=\"190\" y1=\"204\" x2=\"190\" y2=\"240\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><polygon points=\"190,250 196,240 184,240\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\"/><text x=\"150\" y=\"280\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#c0392b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">On bare ground</text><rect x=\"240\" y=\"186\" width=\"140\" height=\"14\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/><rect x=\"284\" y=\"173\" width=\"45\" height=\"13\" rx=\"4.5\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><line x1=\"329\" y1=\"181\" x2=\"361\" y2=\"182\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"7.2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><circle cx=\"275\" cy=\"178\" r=\"8.1\" fill=\"#d9b48f\"/><text x=\"310\" y=\"230\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2e7d32\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Thick bed under</text><text x=\"310\" y=\"250\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#2e7d32\" text-anchor=\"middle\">heat stays in</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"60\" font-size=\"17\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Insulate under you first</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"82\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">then over you</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><aside class=\"callout rule\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Grandpa's rule (wisdom, not law)</div><p>Grandpa's rule (wisdom): When the light turns gold and you are still far from the truck, start building. The dark will not wait for you.</p></aside><aside class=\"callout mistake\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Common mistakes</div><ul><li>Building after dark.</li><li>A roof but no bed.</li><li>Camping in the valley bottom.</li></ul></aside><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: the mistakes in full</summary><ul><li>Starting the shelter after dark. Everything takes 3 times longer by headlamp (Tip).</li><li>A great roof and bare ground under you. The ground wins <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>The valley floor: coldest air, and often wet <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>Under a dead tree (Tip).</li><li>A shelter hidden so well no one can see you. Put orange in the open <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>.</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Tarp step 3: pull the windward edge down to the ground and pin it with rocks or stakes. Open side away from the wind.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">3. Low to the wind</text><rect x=\"0\" y=\"230\" width=\"400\" height=\"70\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/><rect x=\"57\" y=\"198\" width=\"6\" height=\"32\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><polygon points=\"60,70 24,198 96,198\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/><rect x=\"337\" y=\"198\" width=\"6\" height=\"32\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><polygon points=\"340,70 304,198 376,198\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/><polygon points=\"110,150 290,150 330,230 70,230\" fill=\"#4f7a52\"/><line x1=\"390\" y1=\"120\" x2=\"330\" y2=\"154\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><polygon points=\"320,160 334,160 327,148\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\"/><text x=\"370\" y=\"100\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\" text-anchor=\"middle\">wind</text><circle cx=\"80\" cy=\"230\" r=\"8.0\" fill=\"#9a9a8f\"/><circle cx=\"320\" cy=\"230\" r=\"8.0\" fill=\"#9a9a8f\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"288\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Windward edge pinned low</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><aside class=\"callout field\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Do this in the field</div><p>Before the season, pitch your tarp in the backyard or a legal camp spot in under 10 minutes, then sleep one cold night under it with only your day pack kit.</p></aside>","<div class=\"checklist\" data-list=\"fs-sh-ready\"><label class=\"check\"><input type=\"checkbox\" data-key=\"fs-sh-ready:0\"><span>Tarp or emergency bivy in the day pack</span></label><label class=\"check\"><input type=\"checkbox\" data-key=\"fs-sh-ready:1\"><span>10 m of cord</span></label><label class=\"check\"><input type=\"checkbox\" data-key=\"fs-sh-ready:2\"><span>Closed cell foam sit pad</span></label><label class=\"check\"><input type=\"checkbox\" data-key=\"fs-sh-ready:3\"><span>Puffy, toque, spare dry socks</span></label><label class=\"check\"><input type=\"checkbox\" data-key=\"fs-sh-ready:4\"><span>Foil blanket in the pocket kit</span></label><label class=\"check\"><input type=\"checkbox\" data-key=\"fs-sh-ready:5\"><span>Practised the tarp in under 10 minutes</span></label></div>","<div class=\"tbl\"><table><thead><tr><th>Hook</th><th>Means</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Bed first, roof second</td><td>Ground steals the most heat</td></tr><tr><td>Gold light, start building</td><td>Begin an hour before dark</td></tr><tr><td>Bench, not bottom</td><td>Cold air pools low</td></tr><tr><td>Look up</td><td>No dead trees overhead</td></tr><tr><td>Low to the wind</td><td>Pin the windward edge</td></tr><tr><td>Eat, pee, socks, toque</td><td>Night routine</td></tr><tr><td>Orange in the open</td><td>Stay findable</td></tr></tbody></table></div><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: why these</summary><ul><li>\"Bed first, roof second\" is opinion based on conduction physics (Tip, 75% for the physics).</li><li>\"Bench, not bottom\": cold air drains into low ground at night <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li></ul></details>","","<ul><li>Most shelter technique is hunter and bushcraft practice (Tip). Physics and hypothermia care: Wilderness Medical Society <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: all sources</summary><ul><li><a href=\"https://www.aafp.org/pubs/afp/issues/2020/1101/p571.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">American Family Physician: Accidental hypothermia, Wilderness Medical Society guidelines (2020)</a>, read directly (insulation and vapour barrier, ground contact). Checked 2026-10-11 <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span></li><li><a href=\"https://www.trailhiking.com.au/safety/how-to-build-a-survival-shelter/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Trail Hiking Australia: emergency shelter use and insulation from the ground</a>, checked 2026-10-11 (search preview) <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span></li><li><a href=\"https://www.thegreatoutdoorsmag.com/skills/a-night-in-the-woods-how-to-build-a-woodland-shelter/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">The Great Outdoors: a night in the woods, building a woodland shelter</a>, checked 2026-10-11 (search preview) <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">60%</span></li><li><a href=\"https://www.tsgassociates.co.uk/news/item/mylar-blankets-fall-short-in-hypothermia-treatment\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">TSG Associates: Mylar blankets fall short in hypothermia treatment</a>, checked 2026-10-11 (search preview) <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span></li><li><a href=\"https://outdoors.codidact.com/q/58097\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Outdoors Codidact: do emergency space blankets work?</a>, checked 2026-10-11 (search preview, forum) <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">60%</span></li><li>Hunt Mentor: <a href=\"#/s/wind-thermals/0\">Wind and thermals</a> for evening cold air drainage <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span></li></ul></details>"]